The beginning of May.%K%P
五月上旬%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dOh? You worked at Kamata Trading?\d%K%P
「喔，之前在镰田商事工作？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dY-Yes. I spent about five years there.\d%K%P
「额，嗯。在那工作了大概五年」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dBut that's a top level corporation, nothing like our\nhumble organization here! I hear they had some trouble\nwith fraud or whatnot last year, but now they're back at\nfull strength!\d%K%P
「和我们公司不一样，那是个大企业啊！\n听说去年发生了点小危机，\n但现在也算是恢复得像模像样了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dY-You're exaggerating... Ah, I mean, that's just how able\ntheir employees were...\d%K%P
「倒、倒也没有那么夸张…啊，不，\n大家都是很敬业，非常优秀的人」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dI don't doubt that. Unlike my place, you've got alumni\nfrom top universities going straight to your door.\n...Which reminds me, you're a graduate of Yatsubashi,\naren't you?\d%K%P
「也是啊，毕竟和我们公司不一样，他们公司都是些一流大学毕业的优秀人才。…说起来芳村先生也是八桥大学毕业的？」※译注：八桥大学，原型为一桥大学，丸户作品里出现频率最高的大学。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dY-Yes, but...\d%K%P
「我、我也不是那么…」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dStraight to Kamata after Yatsubashi, huh. The life path\nof an social elite if I've ever heard one. But then why\nwould someone of your qualifications quit and apply with\nus?\d%K%P
「八桥毕业到镰田工作，应该就能一路成为社会精英啊。\n…但为什么要从镰田辞职到我们公司应聘？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dTh-That's...\d%K%P
「额…那、那是…」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dDid you fall ill, perhaps? I hear they drive their\nemployees quite hard over there.\d%K%P
「难道是身体吃不消？\n听说那的工作都忙不完」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh? Ah! Th-That's ri--?!\d%K%P
「诶？啊！\n就、就是那………！？」%K%P
\dYou shouldn't make up negative stuff like quitting your\njob because of an illness. Being honest and admitting you\nwere fired would be for the best.\d%K%P
『“患有疾病”这种消极思想是无法圆谎的。\n还是老老实实地说“被裁员了”比较好！』%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dI hear about people collapsing from mental stress these\ndays. Ours is a small place, so the amount of work one has\nto manage is in no way meager...\d%K%P
「最近因为心理原因病倒的人很多。\n我们公司因为规模小，每个人的工作量都是相当大的…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dN-No! It's not like that! I'm used to being busy! I'm\nconfident in both my stamina and spirit!\d%K%P
「不，不会的！我已经习惯忙碌了。\n我对自己的体力和毅力都有自信！」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dOh, is that so? Did you participate in any sports back in\nschool?\d%K%P
「喔，这样啊。\n你在学生时代有参加过什么体育运动吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I played volleyball.\d%K%P
「………打排球」%K%P
Once, during a school festival.%K%P
在校内球技大会上。%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dAhh, no wonder, then! I bet the team appreciated your\nheight!\d%K%P
「嗯，果然啊！\n毕竟身高在这摆着。想必一定表现活跃吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHa... Haha...\d%K%P
「哈、哈哈…」%K%P
I didn't do too badly, considering I just stood next to\nthe net with my hands raised.%K%P
好像只有在网前伸直手站着，\n基本上也算是活跃吧…%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dAnyway, let's get to the heart of the matter. Why did you\nchoose our company?\d%K%P
「嘛，那我就开始提问了。\n首先，你想到本公司就职的理由是？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dU-Um... That's... Ah.\d%K%P
「诶，那个，那是因为…啊」%K%P
\dKeep your back straight! Look the people you're talking\nto in the eye! It's gonna give a bad impression if you\nkeep mumbling like you always do. And be careful not to\nsqueak, okay?\d%K%P
『把背挺直！好好将脸正对着对方！\n要是你表现出平常那种低声下气的样子，是会留下坏印象的。\n还有，要注意不要话说一半就咽下去了』%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d(Hahh... Phew...)\d%K%P
「…（吸气～，呼气～）」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dUm, Mr. Yoshimura...?\d%K%P
「芳村先生？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI quit my old company because I felt like I was starting\nto lose my individual sense of worth while working for\nsuch a massive corporation.\d%K%P
「我从以前工作的公司辞职，是因为在人多的组织里，\n我感受不到自己的价值」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dOh?\d%K%P
「喔？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI want to know the faces of the customers I'm serving. I\nbegan to wish for a workplace that would utilize my\nindividual talents better, and thought that Kamata Trading\nmight not have been the best place for me after all.\d%K%P
「我想要做独立接待更多客户的工作。\n更具体地说，我想在能追求个人业绩的职场上工作，\n这样的想法越来越抑制不住了…」%K%P
All right, it seemed like I managed to say that without\nstuttering. This just might be my day.%K%P
好…说得像流水一样顺畅。\n今天…说不定能行。%K%P
I had yesterday's half-day practice interview to thank for\nthat. I'd better buy her something if I successfully land\nthis job.%K%P
这些全都是半天模拟面试的成果啊。\n要是应聘成功的话，必须得好好感谢她啊。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
On the other hand, I wasn't sure how to feel about being\ntaught interview techniques by a schoolgirl. I mean, I've\nbeen a working adult for five years now.%K%P
虽然作为社会人士生活了五年以上的我，倒也不是没有\n“竟然被年级比自己小的女学生传授了找工作的心得，这算什么啊”\n这种想法就是了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWell then, Ms. Kouno! Goodbye!\d%K%P
「那香野老师，再见～」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dAh, Ms. Hinosaka, wait!\d%K%P
「啊，阳坂同学，等一下！」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHuh?\d%K%P
「诶？」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dI'm sorry, but there's something I'd like to ask you.\d%K%P
「抱歉。\n我有件事想问问你」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dToday's not cleaning day.\d%K%P
「今天没有轮到我值日打扫卫生吧？」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dJust give me a few seconds. Please.\d%K%P
「只是一小会，可以吧？不行吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
%XS10\dBut they're having a sale on toilet paper right about now...\d %XE%K%P
「但今天是卫生纸大减价…」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dYou always rush out of the classroom the moment the bell\nrings. I've never been able to have a proper conversation\nwith you.\d%K%P
「阳坂同学总是一放学就直接回家呢。\n总是找不到和你说话的机会」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
%XS10\dUgh, Rinko and Matsuri are leaving ahead of me! It's a one-per-\nperson sale... They're gonna run out...\d %XE%K%P
「啊～，伦子和真鹤都已经走了啊～。\n明明一位顾客只能限买一卷的～」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dSo, could you spare me a minute, Ms. Hinosaka?\d%K%P
「行么？拜托了，阳坂同学」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...What is it?\d%K%P
「………什么事？」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dA-Ah... We'll be done in a heartbeat. I wanted to discuss\nthe way you filled out last week's questionnaire about\nadvancing your studies.\d%K%P
「啊，那、那个…那我就长话短说了。\n是关于上周你交给我的毕业志愿调查的事情」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...Ahh.\d%K%P
「………啊～」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dDon't you think it's a bit too early to make that\ndecision? You still have a whole year ahead of you.\d%K%P
「…现在就得出那样的结论，是不是太早了些？\n还有一年时间啊」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
%XS10\dThen why give out a stupid questionnaire so early? There's still a\nwhole year before it'll matter, anyway.\d %XE%K%P
「您要是真这么想就不该这么早就问我。\n明明还有一年时间的」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dEh?\d%K%P
「诶？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI've got some family circumstances, and I figured it\nwould be best for me to start working as soon as\npossible.\d%K%P
「不，也是由于家里有些事情，\n我想早点进入社会…」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dYour grades are pretty good, and if you keep doing as\nwell as you are, you could easily get into any school you\nwanted.\d%K%P
「阳坂同学你的成绩也很好。\n像这样努力下去的话，不管是私立还是公立的学校，\n大多数你都可以随便挑吧」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dLike I said, I have some family circumstances, okay?\d%K%P
「都说了，现在我家没有那么阔绰…」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dWell, I agree that it could be beneficial to enter\nsociety and learn how the world works, but I don't think\nit's something you should rush.\d%K%P
「嘛，虽然积累社会经验无疑是好事，\n但是啊，我觉得那和现在不做就无法再做的事情\n还是有些许不同的吧」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dLook, I answered your question, but you're not even\nlistening.\d%K%P
「是您说有事想问我才留下的，\n结果您也没有把我的话听进去啊」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dEh?\d%K%P
「诶？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI want to start working as soon as possible so I can make\nlife easier for Mo-- I mean, my mother. Is that such a bad\nthing?\d%K%P
「我想早点独立，\n让妈…让母亲轻松一些。\n这样也不行吗？」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dRight... You were living alone with your mother, weren't\nyou?\d%K%P
「说起来，\n阳坂同学是和妈妈两个人一起生活的啊」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
%XS10\dYes... At least until recently.\d %XE%K%P
「是的………直到最近」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dSpeaking of your mother, she's the only one I've yet to\nreceive a reply from about the parent-teacher conference.\d%K%P
「说起你的妈妈，我想起来了，监护人座谈会的\n调查表就只剩下你的没有上交给我了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dSh-She's so busy she even works weekends!\d%K%P
「她工作很忙，别说平时了，就连周六都在工作！」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dIf she can't afford to drop by in person, I can make a\nhome visit. I don't mind if it's a bit late, either.\d%K%P
「如果没有时间来这的话，我去家访也是可以的。\n当然了，晚上也没问题」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dSh-She's been so busy she doesn't even have time to come\nhome!\d%K%P
「最近忙得连回家的时间都没了！」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dI-Is that true?!\d%K%P
「忙、忙到那种程度了吗？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dY-Yes... So, even if you came to my house right now...\d%K%P
「是、是的…所以就算您来家访也…」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dThat doesn't sound good. So you're alone each night? I\nhave to do something about this... I'm sorry for not\nnoticing sooner. I will make sure to talk to your mother.\d%K%P
「这就是问题了。阳坂同学晚上也是一个人？\n不想办法做点什么是不行的了…抱歉我没注意到。\n近期一定要让我和你母亲谈谈」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「诶…？」%K%P
%LCMs. Kouno
%LC香野老师
\dIn any case, I've heard enough. I'll try writing a letter\nto your mother sometime soon. Stay safe, okay?\d%K%P
「今天就这样吧。\n我会在近期给你母亲寄信联系的。\n那就这样，回家路上小心。」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
%XS10\dShe'd be a great teacher, if only I wasn't in such a messy\nsituation...\d %XE%K%P
「如果不是因为情况特殊，\n她还真是个非常好的老师啊…」%K%P
%LCMan in Black
%LC黑衣男子
\dWelcome home, Milady.\d%K%P
「欢迎回来，大小姐」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dYou don't need to waste your breath on greetings. Rather,\nI'd like to see your report.\d%K%P
「招呼就不用打了。\n先把调查报告书拿给我看看」%K%P
%LCMan in Black
%LC黑衣男子
\dHere you go...\d%K%P
「请看…」%K%P
%LCMan in Black
%LC黑衣男子
\dHinosaka Honoka, the manager of the Terrace House\nHinosaka on East Hagimori 3-24, has been missing since\nmid-March.\d%K%P
「东荻守三丁目２４番地『Terrace House阳之坂』的房东，阳坂穗香，\n自三月中旬起下落不明。」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dNo way...\d%K%P
「怎么回事…」%K%P
%LCMan in Black
%LC黑衣男子
\dAccording to the testimony of her former employer, she\nhad entered into a relationship with a man of unknown\norigin around the start of the year. It is highly probable\nthat he is related to her disappearance.\d%K%P
「据她之前工作的餐饮店“卡特蕾亚”的店长所说，\n从年初开始她就和一个男人关系密切，\n所以会不会是因为那个男人缠上她了…」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dHave you managed to track him down?\d%K%P
「那，现在那个男人的踪迹掌握到了吗？」%K%P
%LCMan in Black
%LC黑衣男子
\dNo. He went missing around the same time. ...To make\nmatters worse, trying to look him up has presented us with\nyet another problem.\d%K%P
「不知道。他们几乎是同时行踪不明的。\n…而且这个男人的背景也有很多问题」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dThis is...\d%K%P
「………这是怎么回事」%K%P
%LCMan in Black
%LC黑衣男子
\dWe would likely only be able to locate Hinosaka Honoka\nafter she either severs her ties with this man, or...\d%K%P
「阳坂穗香再出现的话，\n是完全与这个男人切断了联系，还是…」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dDon't even think about finishing that sentence, Sasaki.\d%K%P
「不要跟我说这些没根没据的事，佐佐木」%K%P
%LCSasaki
%LC佐佐木
\dD-Do forgive me.\d%K%P
「啊，非常抱歉」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dDamn, I wouldn't have gone overseas if I'd known this\nwould happen. If only I had been here at the time...\d%K%P
「早知如此，我就不去留学了。\n要是有我在的话，这点事…」%K%P
%LCSasaki
%LC佐佐木
\dMilady...\d%K%P
「大小姐…」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dThis is my responsibility. I should've at least assigned\nsurveillance in my absence. I really messed up this\ntime...\d%K%P
「不，这是我的责任。\n要是预先派谁去监视一下就好了。\n真是致命的疏忽啊…」%K%P
%LCSasaki
%LC佐佐木
\dYes.\d%K%P
「是的」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dHuh? Are you blaming me now? What was I supposed to do?!\nI couldn't have known something like this would happen!\d%K%P
「什么啊？想说是我的错么？这不是没办法吗！\n事情变成这样无论是谁都想不到的吧！？」%K%P
%LCSasaki
%LC佐佐木
\dM-My apologies.\d%K%P
「非、非常抱歉」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dWell, whatever. But she's still living in that house,\nright? I'm glad I wasn't too late on that account, at\nleast.\d%K%P
「嘛，算了。\n不过，现在那姑娘还留在那个家里吧？\n赶上了，太好了…」%K%P
%LCSasaki
%LC佐佐木
\dYes.\d%K%P
「是的」%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\dLet's go, Sasaki. This time, we're gonna get her to agree\nto our terms. I mean, that's why I came back here in the\nfirst place!\d%K%P
「走吧，佐佐木…\n这回一定要让那姑娘点头。\n我就是为此而回来的」%K%P
%LCSasaki
%LC佐佐木
\dIndeed... Good luck, Milady.\d%K%P
「是…请您慢走，小姐」\n※译注：出自《女仆咖啡巧克拉》ｃｕｒｉｏ店的问候方式。%K%P
%LCLady
%LC大小姐
\d...Um, that didn't sound quite right, did it?\d%K%P
「…是不是有什么地方搞错了？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dTh-Then...\d%K%P
「那、那就…？」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dYeah, do you think you could show up by the start of next\nweek? I'm sorry for the short notice, but we're severely\nundermanned.\d%K%P
「嗯，下周一开始上班可以吧？\n这么着急真是抱歉，我们公司人手不够啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNo, you mustn't apologize! I can do it! I can start today\nif necessary!\d%K%P
「不、不用说什么抱歉的…\n没问题！今天开始上班都行！」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dHahaha, I can't take you in today. I still have some\npaperwork to sort out.\d%K%P
「哈哈，今天是不行的哦。\n我这的接收手续还没整理好」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI-I'm sorry... I just couldn't contain my joy.\d%K%P
「对、对不起…不小心高兴过头了」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dAh, and I said we'd hire you, but the first three months\nare going to be a trial period. After that, if we're all\non the same page, we'll hire you as a full-fledged\nemployee.\d%K%P
「啊啊，还有，虽说是聘用你了，\n但前三个月作为试用期可以的吧？\n那之后，如果符合标准，就正式聘用你」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYes. Of course. As long as you give me something to do.\d%K%P
「好的，本应如此。\n只要让我工作就好…」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dI have high expectations for you, Mr. Yoshimura. Anyway,\nI've got to run...\d%K%P
「期待你的表现，芳村先生。\n接下来，我就出门了…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, I'm sorry for taking up so much of your time.\d%K%P
「啊，抱歉…\n占用您这么长时间」%K%P
%LCPresident of Houei Commerce
%LC邦永商会社长
\dDon't worry about it, kid. Anyway, I hope to see you here\nnext week.\d%K%P
「哪里的话，没关系的。\n那，下周开始就拜托了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dO-Of course! I am looking forward to working with you!\d%K%P
「好、好的！\n请多指教！」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
