%LC理
\d...Heh.\d%K%P
「…呵」%K%P
...%K%P
……%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHeh heh...\d%K%P
「呵呵…」%K%P
...%K%P
…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAhahahaha... Y-Yes! Yes!!\d%K%P
「啊哈哈哈哈…\n成、成功了，成功了…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHurray! I did it!! I did iiiiiiiit!!! I'm hired! I have a\njob now!\d%K%P
「成功了，成功了…\n成功了啊啊啊～！\n聘用了，聘用了，聘用啦～！」%K%P
%LCOffice Lady
%LC女文员
\dSeriously, why now? This is like the worst timing ever.\d%K%P
「为什么现在来应聘…时机不对啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYes, yes, yes...! I'm no longer Mr. Laid-off... Honor\nrestored!\d%K%P
「太好了，太好了…\n丢掉失业者的名号…重新回到社会上来！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAhahahaha... AHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA!!\d%K%P
「哈哈哈哈…啊哈哈哈哈～！」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Huh? Was someone here?\d%K%P
「…咦？有谁来过么？」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dAll right then, our pizza, fries, pasta, and fried\nchicken have just arrived! Mr. Retired, Kuma, clear some\nspace on the table.\d%K%P
「好～嘞，披萨、薯条、意大利面还有炸鸡到了～。\n老爷子～、小熊～，把桌子拉到中间来～」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dOh, finally. Kuma, take care of the other end.\d%K%P
「好，来了。熊先生赶紧把你那里收拾一下」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dWow, that smells great. All this greasy food sure makes\none's appetite go through the roof.\d%K%P
「喔～，闻起来很香啊。\n这些高卡路里的东西让人看着就想吃～」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHold your horses. Did you seriously order nothing but\njunk food?\d%K%P
「喂，等等。\n为什么买了这些垃圾食品啊…」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dWell, I mean, that's pretty much the extent of what you\ncan get from a pizza place.\d%K%P
「这个嘛，\n因为这就是披萨屋外卖能送来的最多程度了」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI can't believe you people eat stuff like this all the\ntime. I should've made something myself...\d%K%P
「真亏你们天天吃这种对身体不好的东西也能受得了啊。\n看来还是得我来做饭…」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dAh, but this is all according to Laid-off's wishes.\d%K%P
「不，今天是失业的要求买的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm, could we maybe stop using that nickname...?\d%K%P
「不，那个绰号就别再…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou can't keep eating like this, Mr. Laid-off. There's no\nway you're getting proper nourishment. It affects your\nheight, you know.\d%K%P
「失业先生…这种食物是不行的哦。\n总吃这种东西对长身体是不利的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh... I-I'm sorry. Italian cuisine is one of the few\nthings I truly like, so I couldn't resist.\d%K%P
「啊…对、对不起。\n意大利面是我为数不多的喜欢吃的食物之一，\n所以不小心就…」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dYou sure about the height thing?\d%K%P
「对长身体不利…谁的？」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dOh, hold your tongue, kid. The Young Mistress is in the\nright on all accounts. But, as always, reality is a cruel\nmistress.\d%K%P
「别这么说嘛。\n小房东说的从理论上来说是没错，\n只是现实总是很残酷的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhat's up with you, anyway? How can you be unable to eat\nany Japanese cooking other than fried stuff? How did they\nraise you over there? Are you sure you're Japanese? Is\nGifu really a part of our country?\d%K%P
「再说了，吃不了米饭就算了，但就连除了油炸食品\n之外的和食都不能吃，你究竟是怎么被养大的啊？\n你真是日本人么？本州岐阜县的？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI-It's located at the very center, actually. We don't\neven border the sea... I'm sorry.\d%K%P
「基、基本上在那正中了。\n诶诶，四面都没有海…对不起」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dI feel like both of them should apologize to our proud\nnation.\d%K%P
「你们两个好像越说越偏离原话题了…」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dI think Hooba Miso goes well with rice, personally.\d%K%P
「拌着朴叶酱什么的试着吃点饭吧」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dWell, well, Young Mistress, let the poor boy off the hook\nonce in a while. I mean, today is a special day for him.\d%K%P
「算了算了，小房东。这种事就先放一边吧。\n今天嘛，是小少爷可喜可贺的日子」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dIt isn't like I'm not happy for him, okay? It's just\nthat, when I look at Mr. Laid-off, I can't help but worry\nif he'll really be able to do his job properly.\d%K%P
「我又…又没有不高兴。\n只不过，看到失业先生这个样子，\n我真担心他能不能好好在公司工作啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell, I think I was doing fine for five years until\n'that' happened...\d%K%P
「再怎么说到去年为止我也是工作了五年的…」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dYeah, uh, hold that thought! Let's continue after a\ntoast.\d%K%P
「啊～好了好了！\n暂且继续下去吧，来干杯，干杯！」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dRight. You gotta dig in while it's hot.\d%K%P
「是啊是啊，饭就是要趁热吃啊」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dWell then, it seems like the preparations are over, so\nallow me... There's no line of work that leads to easy\nriches. And among all clerks, those in trade -- in other\nwords, salesmen -- have it the hardest.\d%K%P
「那么～这准备得也都差不多了…\n工作挣钱不是件轻松容易的事。\n工薪族尤其是很辛苦的，简短来说…」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dYou're gonna put us to sleep, dude.\d%K%P
「开场白就算了吧，开场白」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dLaid-off! You've got ten seconds to give us a toast!\d%K%P
「失业者，带头干杯啊。１０秒以内！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh? A-All right! Then, uh, um... I got a job! Thank you\nfor your support, everyone! Cheers!\d%K%P
「诶？好、好的！\n那，那么，额，那个………我成功就职了！\n非常感谢大家！干～杯！」%K%P
%LCEveryone
%LC全员
\dCheers!\d%K%P
「干～杯！」%K%P
Our paper cups and beer cans touched with a sound I\ncouldn't in good conscience call pleasant.%K%P
纸杯和啤酒罐互相碰撞着，\n发出不怎么优美的声音，\n满溢的酒撒到了桌子上还有地板上。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThank you... from the bottom of my heart. I truly mean\nthat.\d%K%P
「谢谢…\n真的很感谢大家…」%K%P
Once everyone had taken their respective sips, I received\nthe warmest applause in my life.%K%P
仿佛尽在不言，\n只需将心意连同啤酒泡沫一同灌进肚子里，\n然后，我被四个人的温暖掌声包围…%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAnyway, now that we're done with the toast, I'd like to\nreturn to the matter at hand and remind you that from now\non, you'll have to wake up at 7AM every morning. And I\ncan't guarantee I'll be back by that time.\d%K%P
「那，杯也干完了，接着说刚才的事，\n从下周开始就必须每天早上７点起床了哦？\n要是能赶上我送完报纸回来的话那倒还好…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThe first thing you'll have to buy after receiving your\nsalary is an alarm clock. Oh... maybe we could use that\none with pictures lying around at Mr. Kumazaki's place.\d%K%P
「发工资了首先要去买个闹钟啊。\n啊…熊崎先生那有很多带插画的，还是算了吧」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dNo way! It cost me a fortune, with pre-recorded voices\nand all!\d%K%P
「不行啊！\n那个可是带配音的老贵了！」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
I tried to savor the joy of finally becoming a full-\nfledged resident of Terrace House Hinosaka, but...%K%P
我倒是很愿意仔细品味一下成为\n『Terrace House阳之坂』一员的幸福就是了…%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dHouei Commerce? Never heard of it.\d%K%P
「邦永商会…没听说过啊」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dThe right side has neither.\d%K%P
「同意右面的」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dNeither has the right side.\d%K%P
「同意对面的」\n※译注：麻将用语。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm, mahjong positions don't make much sense with five\npeople here...\d%K%P
「不，今天有五个人，那种位置关系也…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhat are you all talking about? It's in the newspaper.\nJust look at the help wanted section.\d%K%P
「说什么呢。报纸上有刊登啊！\n…看，在这个招聘栏里」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dAh, I see it now. It was so small I totally missed it.\d%K%P
「啊～真的啊。\n…虽然不怎么起眼」%K%P
Actually, I kind of contacted them because of that ad.%K%P
不过，也正是看到了这个我才去应聘的。%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dOffice furniture and automation wholesale...?\d%K%P
「业务·ＯＡ机器的销售…？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt's a small company selling stationery, desks, chairs,\nand other things for office use.\d%K%P
「主要是向中小企业销售\n文具、桌子椅子这样的办公用品，\n是个很小的公司」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dI wonder if it's gonna go well. Are you sure you can\nmanage a sales job?\d%K%P
「没问题吧？\n小少爷你能胜任营销工作么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI-I'm going to be fine... I think. I mean, I'm sure. I\noriginally come from a trading corporation, after all.\d%K%P
「没、没问题的…大概，不，一定。\n我原来工作的公司就是商业公司」%K%P
Although my job was mainly general affairs and accounting.%K%P
只不过干的是行政还有财务。%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dWell, at least no one will ever get angry at you for\ngetting out of line, I guess.\d%K%P
「嘛，这态度太高傲了\n永远都会惹人生气的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dRemember, Mr. Laid-off, you've got to look whoever you're\ntalking to in the eye. And while it helps to know how to\napologize, you shouldn't do it all the time. Otherwise, no\none will buy your sincerity when it really counts.\d%K%P
「知道吗，失业先生。跟人说话时要好好看着对方的眼睛。\n还有，虽然道歉确实很重要，但总是道歉就不好了。\n否则等到真要低头的时候就表现不出来诚意了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dR-Right. I'll be careful. I'm sorry...\d%K%P
「是、是的，我会注意的，对不起…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAnd there you go with the apologies again! In this\nsituation, gratitude was more important than amends, don't\nyou think?\d%K%P
「你看你看，刚才的『对不起』就不用说！\n刚才那种情况，重要的是感谢，而不是道歉吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, I see... Thank you, Mitoko.\d%K%P
「啊，这样啊………\n谢谢你，美都子」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dR-Right... Just like that.\d%K%P
「对、对…就是这样」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dHow come I don't feel an age gap between those two?\d%K%P
「这俩在一块怎么看不出来年龄的差距啊…」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\d...If anything, Mitoko comes off as the older one.\d%K%P
「…倒不如说，感觉上美都子妹妹反而年长一些」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh, no! That one's recyclable, so it should go here!\d%K%P
「啊，不对。那个是可再生垃圾，放到这边」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh... I'm sorry.\d%K%P
「啊…对不起」%K%P
Our little party came to an end at about 10PM that night.%K%P
晚上１０点已过，\n我的庆祝会圆满结束了。%K%P
Mr. Retired and the others weren't too thrilled about\nfinishing so early, but Mitoko had to wake up at 3AM\ntomorrow, so any longer and it would have pretty much\nturned into an all-nighter for her.%K%P
老爷子他们表现出了意犹未尽的不满，\n但美都子明天凌晨３点就要起床，\n所以现在已经属于是在熬夜了。%K%P
And it wasn't like I couldn't hang out with them some\nother day. Or rather, they would invite me to a party at\nleast once every three days.%K%P
嘛，那帮人的话，反正随时都有机会。\n倒不如说三天不邀请人聚会就有问题了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dOkay, so this one is for Monday, and this other one is\nfor Tuesday. Don't forget to get them out before 9AM. But\nbe careful not to leave the trash out in the open too\nearly or it'll attract crows.\d%K%P
「好了…额。那这边是周一，这边是周二。\n好好记着别忘了早上９点之前出门哦？\n太早出门是会有乌鸦过来的，要小心啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOkay. I understand.\d%K%P
「好的，我明白了」%K%P
Mitoko was cleaning up the scene of carnage left in the\nwake of our party with almost uncanny precision and speed.%K%P
大家各自回房间之后，美都子干净利落地\n进行了『士兵的梦之迹』的战后处理。\n※译注：『士兵的梦之迹』出自松尾芭蕉所著《深处的细道》。%K%P
My room -- littered with dozens of empty cans, paper cups,\nand plates -- had returned to its usual empty state in a\nmatter of minutes.%K%P
直到刚才还被空罐子塑料杯纸杯纸碟子填满的我的房间\n一瞬间就恢复到了跟平常一样什么都没有的状态。%K%P
...Which was a bit of a depressing sight, actually.%K%P
…嘛，虽然从另一方面来说着实让人感到有点寂寞。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWell, I guess I shouldn't worry about your trash anymore.\nI mean, we'll be waking up at the same time starting next\nweek, anyway.\d%K%P
「嘛…不过从下周开始扔垃圾也许就没问题了。\n毕竟每天早上都可以同时起床了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI suppose...\d%K%P
「是、啊」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...What's wrong?\d%K%P
「…怎么了？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou finally found a job. Congratulations, Mr. Laid-off!\d%K%P
「终于重新就业了。\n恭喜你，失业先生」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh? O-Oh... Thanks.\d%K%P
「诶？啊、啊啊………谢谢」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI'm really happy for you. I bet God noticed how hard you\nwere trying.\d%K%P
「太好了…\n你的努力都被神明看到了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dMitoko...\d%K%P
「美都子…」%K%P
She was pretty tough on me in front of others, but the\nmoment we were left alone, her attitude shifted to that of\ngenuine kindness.%K%P
大家都在时她从来都是指责我，让我难堪，\n只有现在，两个人独处之时，\n她会放下愚弄和冷漠，对我说着温柔的话语。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAnd try to handle things better this time, so you don't\nfail again. It's important to give your all for the\ncompany and so on, but no one's gonna blame you if you try\nto be a little bit more selfish, okay?\d%K%P
「这次要多抓住些要领，可别再失败了哦？\n公司的利益虽然也很重要，但稍微以自己为中心去做事\n也是不会遭到报应的啊，知道了吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
Not for too long, though.%K%P
只不过是我单方面不知道如何说下去就是了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAnd here you go falling silent and looking at the ground\nagain. That's gonna give your customers a bad impression,\nokay? I'm really starting to worry about you, Mr. Laid-\noff...\d%K%P
「你看你，又沉默着把头低下去了。\n这样会给客户带来坏印象的吧？\n真的没问题么，失业先生…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dU-Um... Putting aside the question of whether or not I'll\nbe all right... how about we stop using that nickname?\d%K%P
「我、我说啊…有没有问题先不管，\n所以说，那个“失业”，能不能…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAh. That's right...\d%K%P
「啊，这样啊…」%K%P
Everyone celebrated my employment, yet not a single person\nthought to change my nickname.%K%P
大家搞那么大排场来祝贺我再就业，我是很感动，\n但唯独谁也没有把『失业』称呼改过来这一点让我…%K%P
Well, I guess Mr. Retired's \dYoung Master\d was still fine,\nbut... Wait, now that I thought about it, wasn't that\ntitle normally used for a second son in an aristocratic\nfamily, the one who usually had nothing to do?%K%P
嘛，老爷子最初说的『小少爷』倒是不错…\n不，那个在落语里是不工作的废柴富二代代名词，\n所以一点也不好。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dStill... I don't feel like calling you Mr. Yoshimura at\nthis point.\d%K%P
「但是事到如今再叫你芳村先生的话…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm, then how about another nickname? Like... Mr. Employed\nor Mr. Clerk or something?\d%K%P
「再想点别的叫法行不行？？\n额，比如说…公司职员、工薪族什么的」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...You really want to be called something that dull?\d%K%P
「…用这么平淡无奇的称呼，你会开心？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt would still make me feel better than Mr. Laid-off.\d%K%P
「但最起码能从“失业”里被解救出来」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dPfft!\d%K%P
「噗」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAha...\d%K%P
「啊哈…」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAha... Ahaha... That's right... I totally didn't notice\nit until now, but Mr. Laid-off is kinda rude, isn't it.\d%K%P
