%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dPlease stop and cut me some slack, I'm begging you by\nevery God in the book just don't.\d%K%P
「求您原谅我饶恕我这个后辈」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dAhaha... Sorry, I couldn't resist. But, hmm... could you\ngive me some more time? I've gotten too used to calling\nyou Mr. Laid-off over the past month.\d%K%P
「啊哈哈…对不起啊，戏弄你过头了。\n那个…但是啊，你能不能再稍微等等呢。\n这一个月，失业先生这称呼我已经叫习惯了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell, okay, you can take your time. I hope you'll come up\nwith a nicer nickname.\d%K%P
「嗯，嘛，慢慢来也可以…\n你看看能不能换个好一点的称呼？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dOkay, I'll try. Anyway, good night.\d%K%P
「嗯，我会好好想的。\n那，晚安了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dGood night.\d%K%P
「晚安」%K%P
As always, she treated me with a slight air of\nsuperiority, but with genuine kindness.%K%P
她还是老样子，给人一副高高在上的感觉，\n同时又在我眼前伸出一条名为“温柔”的绳子，\n让我一直都坚信，我可以努力着攀到她的身边。%K%P
The hard-working landlord treated me -- a tenant -- like a\nreal friend.%K%P
勤劳的房东小姐，对待房客\n就像对待亲人一样。%K%P
Yet, if you thought about both our situations, it was\npretty clear which one of us had it tougher.%K%P
冷静地将自己和他人的境遇做对比，\n然后到底哪边才值得让自己最该担心的这种矛盾，\n倒是任谁都能明白的。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dPhew...\d%K%P
「唔…」%K%P
I could still smell the fragrance of cheese in my small\nten square meter apartment. And this odor, too, would soon\nbe dispelled by the draft coming through the thin walls.%K%P
六叠大小的房间里残留下些许的奶酪香味。\n只是随着时间的一点点流逝，\n这气味也被从小小间隙里溜进来的风缓缓吹散了。%K%P
Yet, despite the conditions, I could feel that both my\nbody and soul had been revitalized by a sense of\nfulfillment I'd been a stranger to for over a year.%K%P
还好这小小的陈旧房子里\n之前一年很难品味到的充实感倒是识趣地留了下来，\n并慢慢地渗透进我的身体。%K%P
Next week would mark my first step back into society -- my\ngrudge match, if you will.%K%P
下周开始就是第一步…\n我的东山再起之路开始了。%K%P
Today was the farewell party to my old self. All the\nblessings, alcohol, and snacks I received would turn into\nenergy to drive me onwards--;＆（OSA_0341）%K%P
今天的壮行会、\n大家的祝福、酒以及食物，就是我从今往后的能量之源…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh...?!\d%K%P
「啊…！？」%K%P
I forgot to collect the snack money everyone promised\nme...%K%P
托八须永君帮忙买了披萨和酒，\n可是谁也没有找我要钱…%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAll right.\d%K%P
「好…嘞」%K%P
I folded up my futon and got dressed. It was almost 7AM by\nthe time I finished packing.%K%P
被子叠好，衣服换好，\n该带的都整理好，然后就到七点了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI might be a bit early, but whatever.\d%K%P
「有点早了么…嘛，算了」%K%P
It would take about thirty minutes to get from here to the\nHouei Commerce office on foot and by train. Work started\nat 9AM, so I'd be perfectly fine if I left home around\n8AM.%K%P
从这里去邦永商会的话，坐车加上走路共需要３０分钟。\n９点开始上班，所以８点过了再出门也来得及。%K%P
Even so, it was my first day, after all. It wouldn't hurt\nto arrive early and have more time to greet everybody.%K%P
不过，嘛，今天是第一天上班，\n最早去公司跟同事们问好的话，\n肯定没有损失吧。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'll be going, then.\d%K%P
「我出门了」%K%P
I bid farewell to the empty corridor.%K%P
向没有一个人的走廊小声道别。%K%P
I'd been infected by our landlord's politeness to the\npoint that I began acting all well-mannered and proper,\neven toward inanimate objects.%K%P
被房东小姐一丝不苟性格所感召，\n我也养成了不会遗漏这种礼节的习惯。%K%P
Still, as a member of Japanese society, it wasn't\nparticularly a bad habit to have, all things considered.%K%P
但是，嘛，这个习惯\n毫无疑问是社会人非常喜欢的态度。%K%P
I ended up here due to the biggest misunderstanding of my\nlife, but it might very well turn out to be the perfect\nenvironment to heal my anti-social behavior.%K%P
虽然如今的日常是从最差劲的误会发展而来的，\n但从改变了我不愿意融入社会的生活态度这点来看，\n这说不定是个理想的环境…%K%P
...Well, maybe not entirely perfect, but close enough.%K%P
不，倒也没有断言的自信就是了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell then...!\d%K%P
「那么…！」%K%P
I puffed out my chest, raised my head, and took a firm\nstep forward. This was the first day in the life of the\nbrand new Yoshimura Osamu!%K%P
挺胸抬头，迈步向前吧。\n今天新生芳村理前来报到！%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhoa?!\d%K%P
「诶！？」%K%P
The shrill sound of a bicycle brake interrupted my\nthoughts as I passed through the front gate.%K%P
…刚踏出门的一瞬间，\n一声尖锐的刹车声挡住我的去路。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dYou're too early, Mr. Laid-off!\d%K%P
「失业先生，你太早了！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Mitoko?!\d%K%P
「…诶，美都子！？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dI thought I still had plenty of time, but I guess it was\na good idea to hurry home, after all. Hahh... Hahh...\d%K%P
「我本以为时间应该是很充裕的。\n不过以防万一急着赶回来真是太好了…哈、哈啊…」%K%P
She pressed her palms against her knees as she tried to\ncatch her breath.%K%P
她一边上气不接下气地说着话，\n一边把手撑在膝盖上调整着呼吸。%K%P
