Mitoko's palm of incandescent fury stopped five\ncentimeters from my cheek -- apparently, she realized she\nwas acting childish in the middle of her tantrum.%K%P
美都子那包含着怒气的手掌\n在距离我脸颊五厘米的地方勉强停了下来。\n后来再想想，她生气的理由貌似有点孩子气啊。%K%P
But with nothing else there to quell her fury, she vented\nher anger on the front door by slamming it as hard as she\ncould.%K%P
她重重地关上了玄关的门，\n同时留下了她那无名的焦躁感。%K%P
Which kind of resulted in one of the hinges falling off\nand Mitoko going to look for a set of carpentry tools in\nthe shed, her eyes filling with frustrated tears.%K%P
顺带一提，玄关门上的合页因此坏了一个，\n这下子让她不得不带着快要哭泣的表情，\n跑去仓库拿工具准备修理了。%K%P
I'd volunteered to help, but it proved only to add fuel to\nthe fire. She responded angrily, asking if I'd want to\nmess up my first day at work because of her.%K%P
于是我问道『要帮忙吗？』，\n我都忘记了这是自己今天第一次上班，\n于是她心中的怒火烧得更加猛烈…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThe first thing I'm doing with my salary is treating her\nto dinner.\d%K%P
