The twelve complaint calls I answered this morning turned\ninto forty-one by the evening.%K%P
早上上班时间之前的１２个投诉电话\n到现在为止膨胀到了４１个。%K%P
And I'm not even counting the ones that called multiple\ntimes.%K%P
顺便一提，那些第二次打过来催促的电话\n没有算在这个数字之内。%K%P
I was just a new employee who still didn't know left from\nright in this company.%K%P
可是，毕竟我还只是今天刚刚来工作\n什么都不知道的外行啊。%K%P
All I could do was keep apologizing while writing down\neveryone's contact information.%K%P
姑且是把电话都接了，记下了内容和联系人，\n之后就是一个劲地道歉。%K%P
In a way, it was certainly good news that a small company\nlike this had so many clients, but at the same time, I\nfelt like I could spot an ominous black cloud looming\nabove my head.%K%P
在这种小公司里有着比我预期要多得多的客户，\n我也知道这在某种意义上来讲是个喜报，\n但那在我头上漂浮着的乌云究竟是什么啊。%K%P
I mean, not only did the president fail to show up, but I\nnever met a single person other than Ms. Amagi.%K%P
而且今天，社长就算了，但除了面前的天城小姐以外，\n其他职员一个都没看到。%K%P
There were five desks in the room. We couldn't have been\nthe only employees this place had.%K%P
